# ============================================================================
# SKETCHYBAR INTEGRATION - DYNAMIC SPACE SYNCHRONIZATION
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
#   Keep sketchybar space indicators in sync with yabai spaces automatically.
#   Eliminates need for manual sketchybar restarts when creating/destroying spaces.
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
#   1. space_changed: Triggers sketchybar update when you switch between spaces
#   2. space_created: Automatically adds new space indicator to sketchybar
#   3. space_destroyed: Automatically removes space indicator from sketchybar
#
# HISTORY & DEBUGGING NOTES (2026-01-05):
#   Problem 1: Duplicate ctrl+cmd+x keybindings caused spaces to disappear
#     - One binding moved windows to empty spaces
#     - Another binding switched displays
#     - Both executing simultaneously caused race conditions
#     - Fix: Removed display switch binding, kept move-to-empty-space only
#
#   Problem 2: Invalid event subscription "windows_on_spaces"
#     - Original config subscribed to non-existent event
#     - Caused space items to fail creation with errors
#     - Fix: Changed to valid "space_windows_change" event
#
#   Problem 3: Race condition during service restart (ctrl+cmd+0)
#     - Sketchybar would start before yabai was ready
#     - Empty query result → no space items created
#     - Fix: Added retry loop in sketchybarrc (10 attempts × 0.5s = 5s timeout)
#
# GENERALIZED FOR UNLIMITED SPACES:
#   - Works for any number of spaces (1 to 100+)
#   - Uses $YABAI_SPACE_ID environment variable (set by yabai during signal)
#   - No hardcoded limits or assumptions
#
# ============================================================================

# Trigger sketchybar update when switching spaces
/opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m signal --add event=space_changed action="sketchybar --trigger space_change"

# ============================================================================
# SIGNAL: space_created
# ============================================================================
# WHEN: Fires when you create a new space (yabai -m space --create)
# WHAT: Automatically adds corresponding space indicator to sketchybar
# WHY:  Without this, new spaces wouldn't appear until sketchybar restart
#
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES PROVIDED BY YABAI:
#   $YABAI_SPACE_ID - The index of the newly created space
#
# EVENT SUBSCRIPTIONS:
#   - space_change: Updates when you switch to/from this space
#   - space_windows_change: Updates when windows are added/removed
#
# IMPORTANT: Must match the exact format in sketchybarrc:128-138 to ensure
#            consistency between startup-created and dynamically-created spaces
# ============================================================================
/opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m signal --add event=space_created action='
  sid="$YABAI_SPACE_ID"
  sketchybar --add space space.$sid left \
    --set space.$sid space=$sid \
      icon="$sid" \
      icon.font="SF Pro:Medium:13.0" \
      width=3 \
      padding_left=0 \
      padding_right=0 \
      script="$HOME/.config/sketchybar/plugins/space.sh" \
      click_script="/opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m space --focus $sid" \
    --subscribe space.$sid space_change space_windows_change
  sketchybar --trigger space_change
'

# ============================================================================
# SIGNAL: space_destroyed
# ============================================================================
# WHEN: Fires when a space is destroyed (yabai -m space N --destroy)
# WHAT: Automatically removes corresponding space indicator from sketchybar
# WHY:  Without this, destroyed spaces would remain visible until restart
#
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES PROVIDED BY YABAI:
#   $YABAI_SPACE_ID - The index of the destroyed space
#
# NOTE: macOS Sequoia 15+ may restrict space destruction in some scenarios
#       (e.g., can't destroy space if it has windows or is the only space)
# ============================================================================
/opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m signal --add event=space_destroyed action='
  sketchybar --remove space.$YABAI_SPACE_ID
  sketchybar --trigger space_change
'

